        "id": "h33-h33-2-b2-SPACINGresp5pctW15-20261024-f8bada0c",
        "hypothesis": "Respacing the 1883 most kernel-crowded R0 dots (5% of the field) onto uncovered stretches of the same corroborated ridge within 1.5 km extends along-strike coverage of line-like new faults, which the brief's algebra rewards (a dot pays more cheaply against line-like truth), without changing mass, count or geography.",
        "mechanism": "Under DTI = T/(0.2T + 0.2(S-M) + 0.8|G|) with T a max over dots inside the 300 m (3 px) triangular kernel, a dot whose disk is already covered by neighbours pays full mass for almost no credit. Crowding is measured exactly as summed kernel-disk overlap within 6 px; each crowded dot is moved to the eligible support pixel of maximum exact marginal kernel credit at >= 2.8 px (the parent's own thinning distance) from every remaining dot.",
        "non_fault_mimic": "Crowded dots may be real fault complexity -- intersecting or stepping-over splays (the Faulds-style zones where systems sit) genuinely pack dots into one kernel -- and uncovered support stretches may be cover/vegetation gaps, lithologic contacts or drainage lineaments in the H19-5 field rather than unmapped fault. Either mimic makes the move delete signal and add noise at the same time.",
        "predicted_change": "-0.000 DTI (MODEL; plausible interval -0.008 to +0.008; not a score)",
        "predicted_sign_reason": "Exact H19-5 support-credit balance is -87.1 units (removals lose 4232.6, replacements gain 4145.5): local replacements cannot reach the far uncovered support, so the proxy centre is flat-to-negative and the adopted MODEL is -0.000 with no optimism discount (the balance is already negative). Any |live delta| < 0.010 is no evidence by the session rule.",
        "falsifier": "A paired same-week receipt at the 5% dose with delta <= -0.010 rejects local respacing; monotone worsening across 5/10/15% confirms crowded dots were carrying credit, not redundancy. A delta >= +0.010 at any dose falsifies the credit-uniformity headwind (IR90-25) for arrangement edits and reopens kernel-scale respacing."
      }
